# Trivy ignore list — vulnerabilities triaged as not-applicable.
# Format: one CVE per line, optional `# reason` after.
#
# Currently EMPTY, and nothing in the repo invokes trivy today (the wired
# scanners are grype, OSV and govulncheck — see .github/workflows/security.yml).
#
# It previously suppressed CVE-2026-34040, CVE-2026-41567 and CVE-2026-42306
# as daemon-side `github.com/docker/docker` findings. That module is no longer
# in the graph at all — the container provider moved to github.com/moby/moby,
# and `go mod why -m github.com/docker/docker` reports it out — so the triage
# those entries recorded no longer describes anything we ship.
#
# Removed rather than left in place for the same reason the govulncheck
# allowlist was emptied: an inert suppression file is not a harmless one. The
# day someone wires trivy into CI, three CVEs would arrive pre-silenced on a
# rationale that had quietly stopped being true. An entry here should always be
# a decision someone is making now, not one the repo inherited.
